"Arrays and objects are shared, not copied. Use slice when you need a separate array."

function markdown takes prices, reduction
    for i is 1 to length prices
        prices.i is prices.i - reduction
    return prices

function publish takes entry
    entry:status is "published"

prices is 10, 20, 30
sale is markdown (prices:slice run), 2
print "Original first price: " + prices.1
print "Sale first price: " + sale.1
print "Quarter of the second price: " + (prices.2 / 4)

"Without a copy, the function changes the caller's array."
clearance is markdown prices, 5
print "Original after clearance: " + prices.1
print "Same array: " + (clearance = prices)

"Nested arrays are shared too: both rows of original are the same array."
row is 1, 2
original is row, row
edited is original
edited.(1).2 is 99
print "Original nested value: " + ((original.1).2)
print "Other nested row: " + ((original.2).2)
print "Row itself: " + row.2

"Objects inside arrays are shared in the same way."
entry is object
    title is "Prose field notes"
    status is "draft"
entries is (entry,)
other_entries is entries
publish other_entries.1
print "Object status through original array: " + entries.1:status
print "Object status through original variable: " + entry:status

"An empty object can be populated with colon assignments."
audit is object
audit:message is "ready"
audit:meta is object
    verified is true
print "Audit: " + audit:message
print "Verified: " + audit:meta:verified

missing
print "Missing object property is unset: " + (audit:unknown = missing)

"Remainder and mathematical modulo differ for negative operands."
print "Remainder operator: " + (-1 % 26)
print "Prefix remainder: " + (remainder -1 26)
print "Mathematical modulo: " + (-1 mod 26)
